---
description: APPLY rule WHEN using TanStack React Query (v5+) with a **by‑module** architecture (each domain owns its keys/options/queries/mutations)
alwaysApply: false
---

# 🔧 Philosophy

- **Each domain module self‑contains** its React Query pieces: keys, schemas, API fetchers, options builders, hooks (queries & mutations), and local tests.
- **Shared-only** items live in `src/lib/tanstack`: client factory, global typings, HTTP util, (optional) devtools & persistence.
- Encourages **precise invalidation**, easy code‑splitting, and clear ownership.

---

## 🗂️ Project Structure (by module)

```
src/
  modules/
    onboarding/
      api/
        index.ts                  // barrel re-exports for the module
        keys.ts                   // query-key factory (users)
        schema.ts                 // zod schemas & types
        api.ts                    // fetchers (use http util, Zod-validated)
        options.ts                // queryOptions/mutationOptions builders
        queries.ts                // useQuery/useSuspenseQuery hooks
        mutations.ts              // useMutation hooks (optimistic updates)

    clinic/
      api/                   // another domain (same pattern)
        index.ts
        keys.ts
        schema.ts
        api.ts
        options.ts
        queries.ts
        mutations.ts

  lib/
    tanstack/
      client.ts                 // QueryClient factory & exported singleton
      types.ts                  // Global Register typings (keys, error, meta)
      utils/
        http.ts                 // fetch wrapper (AbortSignal + error shape)
      devtools.ts               // (optional) RQ Devtools in dev only
      persist.ts                // (optional) cache persistence setup
```

> **Only** keep generic, cross‑module utilities in `lib/tanstack`. Everything domain‑specific stays inside its module.

